Package: FruitTrait
Type: Package
Title: Colour of Fleshy Fruits from Field Photographs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8401-472X")),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", email = "cjung@gknu.ac.kr", role = "aut"))
Description: Measures the colour of single fleshy fruits in field photographs:
    single photos, folders of photos, folders sorted by species, or photos of
    fruiting observations found through the Global Biodiversity Information
    Facility ('GBIF') and 'iNaturalist'. An optional 'Python' back end finds
    fruits with 'Grounding DINO' in two passes, outlines every single fruit
    with 'Segment Anything' 2.1, rejects outlines that are too small, cut,
    overlapping or clustered, classifies each outlined fruit (single fruit
    with a correct outline, ripe, dry) with logistic classifiers on 'OpenCLIP'
    embeddings, and reports the CIELAB colour of each fruit and of the ripe
    fruits of each photo, with white-balanced colour, colour names and the
    colour of the surroundings. In R, the package reads, filters and
    summarises results, recomputes fruit colour from crops and outlines,
    converts reflectance spectra to the same colour space, checks colour
    casts, corrects white balance, plots outlines and colours, reads the
    tables of the published data set and tells whether a species is in the
    scope of the method (fleshy-fruited trees, shrubs and woody climbers). A
    trait catalogue rates every trait by its repeatability between two photos
    of the same plant (intraclass correlation) and its invariance to
    simulated camera changes and fruit size, and functions are provided to
    repeat these tests and augmentation checks on new photos.
